{"item_id":"E-RES-619","ledger":[{"claim_id":"Q01","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"Turn the abstract topic into a bounded Bareni workflow decision. Explain one practical next step."},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"have a frequent, repeatable workflow with a
  measurable outcome"}],"rationale":"This is a framing instruction and diagnostic question directed at the reader, not an assertion of any current Bareni capability, deployment or observed result. Framing a bounded recurring-workflow choice is consistent with the approved audience definition and the approved task.","use_guidance":"Keep as a framing question and bounded choice. Do not attach any transcript-accuracy figure, cost number or customer example; the friction estimate must stay the reader's own, and the 8-10 hours persona figure must not be presented as a statistic or result."},{"claim_id":"Q02","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"explain one observable workflow decision, threshold, diagnostic question,
  control, or next step"},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Numbers require a source and status. Keep observed results, estimates, targets,
  synthetic data, and examples distinct."}],"rationale":"An instruction to the owner to define accuracy and quantify their own verification cost. It proposes a measurement activity rather than reporting any measured outcome or existing Bareni capability.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly as something the reader measures for themselves. Do not supply example error rates, cost-per-error values or time savings; any illustrative case must be labelled as an example, not an observed result. Invoice line-item extraction may be named only as a workflow type, not as a working transcript/OCR capability."},{"claim_id":"Q03","category":"FORBIDDEN","evidence":[{"source_id":"C03","quote":"PDF/scan ingestion and OCR are not implemented."},{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Bareni currently declines high-sensitivity medical, legal, and financial work;
  bulk cold-email automation; scan-heavy OCR-dependent workflows"}],"rationale":"The core assertion is a current factual claim about how transcript/speech AI performs (works well with clear speakers and standard accents, struggles with poor audio and jargon). No approved source describes any audio transcription or speech-recognition capability or performance for Bareni; the demos cover text-based extraction, vector search and grounded answers only. This is an unsupported performance benchmark, not a limitation that can be added.","use_guidance":"Exclude the performance characterisation. If a fit statement is needed, use only the approved scope discipline: Bareni currently declines high-sensitivity medical, legal and financial work and scan-heavy OCR-dependent workflows, presented as current scope discipline rather than a claim that such work can never be automated. This substitute is not approval of the original accuracy claim."},{"claim_id":"Q04","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Bareni currently declines high-sensitivity medical, legal, and financial work"},{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Present these as
  current scope discipline, not claims that the work can never be automated."},{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Human approval is mandatory for money movement and other high-risk decisions."}],"rationale":"The decision rule itself is permissible and the excluded-scope element has approved support, but the claim as written says automation is 'off the table now' for medical, legal and financial workflows without framing this as Bareni's current scope discipline, and it lists 'legal' among exclusions without noting that Bareni does not give legal advice.","use_guidance":"Add the qualification that these exclusions are Bareni's current scope discipline, not a claim that such work can never be automated, and keep the human-approval boundary explicit for money movement and other high-risk decisions. Do not offer legal advice. Present tolerable error rate and draft-versus-final as the reader's own thresholds, with no suggested numeric values."},{"claim_id":"Q05","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C02","quote":"Normal sequence: free 30-minute diagnostic; free one-page pilot proposal;
  paid working MVP in days; fixed-price pilot in weeks"},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"The diagnostic identifies the one recurring workflow, says honestly whether AI
  fits, and—if it does—defines pilot scope, fixed price, and measures."},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"Customers who want strategy only can buy the separate AI Strategy & Roadmap"}],"rationale":"The free 30-minute diagnostic, honest fit assessment, and fixed-price pilot with measures are supported. However, 'test whether AI accuracy meets your threshold' implies a transcript-accuracy testing capability not evidenced, and 'no multi-month roadmap required' brushes against the separately offered AI Strategy & Roadmap.","use_guidance":"Restate the diagnostic in approved terms only: identify the one recurring workflow, say honestly whether AI fits, and if it fits define pilot scope, fixed price and measures. Remove the implication that accuracy is tested during the diagnostic. Note that timings and scopes are intended, not guarantees, and that a separate AI Strategy & Roadmap exists for strategy-only buyers. This description of the offer is not a CTA; the task authorises none."},{"claim_id":"Q06","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"**CTA rule:** None."},{"source_id":"S01","quote":"final approval and business authority remain human"}],"rationale":"A next-step instruction that leaves the decision with the reader and explicitly avoids a CTA. It asserts no current capability, customer or result.","use_guidance":"Keep as a reader-side next step with no CTA, no booking prompt and no scarcity or urgency language. At most one soft closing sentence; do not include 'Book a free 30-minute diagnostic' or 'Watch the demo'."}]}

